KEPT.poke(p) keeps a view read out of 'me' in the global 'KEPT', which every routine reaches, and the build can't compare those later uses with where that view's place is given back: keep a Stamped of the entity there (its stamp(), read back with fetch(), which fails once the entity has ended), make the field an &E? when one holder keeps the value, or hand the view as an argument to the routines that use it. An Addr (the view's .to[Addr](), turned back with .to[@T?]() and a when) is for links the program keeps right itself, such as a runtime's queues
